  {
   "id": 202,
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Outcome",
   "description": "mph_run_finished{mph_run_id=\"$run\"}. Recorded once at run end and always 1, so the outcome is read from the label, not the value: a missing series means the run has not finished. The mapping is what turns the label into a verdict - ok green, budget_exhausted yellow, error and timeout red.",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "mph-prometheus"
   },
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 3,
    "w": 3,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 2
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "none",
     "decimals": 0,
     "color": {
      "mode": "thresholds"
     },
     "thresholds": {
      "mode": "absolute",
      "steps": [
       {
        "color": "green",
        "value": null
       },
       {
        "color": "yellow",
        "value": 2
       },
       {
        "color": "red",
        "value": 3
       }
      ]
     },
     "mappings": [
      {
       "type": "value",
       "options": {
        "1": {
         "index": 0,
         "text": "ok",
         "color": "green"
        },
        "2": {
         "index": 1,
         "text": "budget_exhausted",
         "color": "yellow"
        },
        "3": {
         "index": 2,
         "text": "error",
         "color": "red"
        },
        "4": {
         "index": 3,
         "text": "timeout",
         "color": "red"
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "",
     "values": false
    },
    "orientation": "auto",
    "textMode": "auto",
    "colorMode": "value",
    "graphMode": "none",
    "justifyMode": "auto"
   },
